Build and link dependencies
---------------------------

These are resolved by find_package at configure time. This repository does not
contain their source, but their code does reach the binaries this project
produces, so a distributed build must carry their licences.

Eigen

    Licence   primarily MPL-2.0; individual files carry their own terms, and
              Eigen's own COPYING.README is the authority on which
    Reached by header inclusion, so Eigen code is compiled into ORVD objects

  Eigen 3.4 is not uniformly MPL-2.0. Most of it is, some files are BSD-3-Clause,
  and some optional backends are offered under LGPL-2.1+ or MPL-2. Upstream
  provides EIGEN_MPL2_ONLY for projects that must exclude the non-MPL2 parts;
  this build does not define it, so the accurate statement is the one above
  rather than a blanket claim. A release that bundles or statically embeds Eigen
  must determine the terms of the files it actually ships.

fmt

    Licence   MIT (Expat)
    Reached by dynamic linking against libfmt

  A package that bundles libfmt must carry the licence text of the fmt version
  it bundles.


